# GlobalSign GCC R46 OV TLS CA 2025 - an intermediate certificate authority,
# vendored so that www.elections.alaska.gov can be read with its chain checked.
#
# Why: the server presents a certificate issued by this CA but sends
# "GlobalSign RSA OV SSL CA 2018" (of the R3 root) with it instead. Browsers
# fetch the missing intermediate from the certificate's Authority Information
# Access; Python does not, so every read failed with CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED
# "unable to get local issuer certificate" on the GitHub runner (daily refreshes
# from at least 2026-10-23). kyc/tls.py adds this file to the default trust
# store's roots: it completes a chain only where GlobalSign Root R46 signs it,
# and certificate and hostname checks stay on (rule 8: never trusted less).
#
# Downloaded 2026-10-26 from the leaf's own AIA "CA Issuers" address:
#   http://secure.globalsign.com/cacert/gsgccr46ovtlsca2025.crt  (DER, converted to PEM)
# Subject:  C=BE, O=GlobalSign nv-sa, CN=GlobalSign GCC R46 OV TLS CA 2025
# Issuer:   C=BE, O=GlobalSign nv-sa, CN=GlobalSign Root R46
# Basic Constraints: critical, CA:TRUE, pathlen:0
# Valid:    2025-09-17 to 2029-06-23
# Serial:   84435890836f67394182cb9c9a5dc99f
# SHA-256:  D1:60:E2:DE:4E:56:CB:10:B6:6C:1C:B0:AD:CB:79:CF:93:C7:8D:CD:9D:B3:0C:20:18:22:02:62:C0:40:63:F9
# SHA-1:    82:F8:D7:11:87:5F:A3:B9:CF:92:01:AB:F6:22:4F:BA:C6:71:27:70
#
# Checked 2026-10-26:
# - it verifies against GlobalSign Root R46 in Mozilla's root store
#   (openssl verify -CAfile <Mozilla ca-bundle.crt> this.pem: OK);
# - the elections.alaska.gov leaf verifies with it and not without it
#   (openssl verify -CAfile <bundle> -untrusted this.pem leaf.pem: OK);
# - GlobalSign's own list of OrganizationSSL intermediates
#   (https://support.globalsign.com/ca-certificates/intermediate-certificates/organizationssl-intermediate-certificates)
#   gives this CA the same serial and the thumbprint
#   82f8d711875fa3b9cf9201abf6224fbac6712770 (SHA-1; the page publishes no SHA-256).
#
# Replace it only with the certificate the leaf's AIA names, checked the same way.
